From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:28:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: probe all regulators at board init

U-Boot probes regulators lazily. Regulators marked regulator-always-on
or regulator-boot-on are probed after bind, but a regulator without
those properties is only probed when something uses it, so its enable
GPIO is never configured.

Recore relies on probing for PD7: its usb0-vbus regulator has neither
property, so probing it drives PD7 low and keeps the board from
sourcing VBUS on the USB-C port. Probe the whole regulator uclass from
board_init() so that every regulator in the device tree gets its
initial state.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
index 3d1afec7..f4d968f8 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@
 #include <axp_pmic.h>
 #include <generic-phy.h>
 #include <phy-sun4i-usb.h>
+#include <dm/uclass.h>
+#include <power/regulator.h>
 #include <asm/arch/clock.h>
 #include <asm/arch/cpu.h>
 #include <asm/arch/display.h>
@@ -231,6 +233,12 @@ int board_init(void)
 
 	eth_init_board();
 
+#if CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(DM_REGULATOR)
+	ret = uclass_probe_all(UCLASS_REGULATOR);
+	if (ret)
+		debug("%s: Cannot probe regulators\n", __func__);
+#endif
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
